{
  "_comment": [
    "Nchito's language layer. The same pattern as taxonomy.json: one source,",
    "generated into every surface.",
    "",
    "HONESTY RULES BAKED INTO THIS FILE",
    "",
    "1. A missing translation is `null`, never a guess. The generator falls back",
    "   to English, and every surface shows English rather than something that",
    "   might be wrong. A mistranslated 'cash out' costs someone real money.",
    "",
    "2. `reviewed: false` on a language means NO NATIVE SPEAKER HAS CHECKED IT.",
    "   These were written from working knowledge, and Zambian usage varies by",
    "   town and by generation. The app says so to the user, in that language's",
    "   own screen, until someone signs it off. Do not flip the flag without a",
    "   real review — it is the only thing standing between a user and a",
    "   confidently wrong instruction about their money.",
    "",
    "3. Coverage is measured, not assumed. `node nchito-shared/generate.mjs`",
    "   prints per-language coverage, and a language below the floor is not",
    "   offered in the picker at all — a half-translated interface reads as",
    "   broken, and broken is worse than English.",
    "",
    "4. Where real Zambian speech uses the English loanword — 'plumbing',",
    "   'electrical', 'delivery' — the translation is deliberately null. That",
    "   is not laziness; inventing a word nobody says is worse than the word",
    "   everybody says."
  ],

  "languages": [
