  "lexicon": {
    "_comment": [
      "Words a person actually types to WhatsApp, mapped to a menu action.",
      "This is the part of 'vernacular' that needs no speech technology at all",
      "and works today: someone types 'ndalama' and lands on their wallet.",
      "Spelling varies wildly in practice, so variants are listed rather than",
      "normalised — matching is substring, case-insensitive, longest-wins.",
      "",
      "Because matching is by substring, a term that is contained in a term",
      "from another bucket silently steals it. The generator fails on that, so",
      "short words like 'hi' are out: 'hi' lives inside 'chilimba'."
    ],
    "gigs":    ["ntchito", "incito", "ncito", "nchito", "mulimo", "musebezi", "gig", "job", "work", "basa"],
    "wallet":  ["ndalama", "indalama", "chikwama", "icikwama", "wallet", "balance", "cash", "money", "kobili", "mali"],
